          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em connection on a 2-bundle
            generalizes the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection on a bundle
            from
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
          %p
            It comes with a notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+parallel+transport"} 2-dimensional parallel transport
          %p
            For an exposition of the concepts here see also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Chern-Weil+theory+introduction"} infinity-Chern-Weil theory introduction
            the section
            %em
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/infinity-Chern-Weil%20theory%20introduction#ConnectionOn2Bundle"} Connections on principal 2-bundles
            \.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-group"} Lie 2-group
            %em connection
            on a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            coming from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : X \to \mathbf{B}G
            is a lift of the cocycle to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid+of+Lie+2-algebra+valued+forms"} 2-groupoid of Lie 2-algebra valued forms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{conn}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mi conn
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mo ∇
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}G_{conn}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\nabla}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                  }
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#on_trivial_2bundles On trivial 2-bundles
          %p
            When the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is topologically trivial, then the connections on it are identified with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-algebra+valued+differential+forms"} Lie 2-algebra valued differential forms
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p Recall from the discussion there what such form data looks like.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            be some
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-algebra"} Lie 2-algebra
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+2-group"} derivation Lie 2-algebra
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_0
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_1
            be the two vector spaces involved and let
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{t^a\} \,, \;\;\; \{b^i\}
          %p
            be a dual basis, respectively. The structure of a Lie 2-algebra is conveniently determined by writing out the most general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi cdgAlg
                    %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CE(\mathfrak{g}) \in cdgAlg_\mathbb{R}
          %p with these generators.
          %p We thus have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi c
                  %mo −
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{CE(\mathfrak{g})} t^a = - \frac{1}{2}C^a{}_{b c} t^b \wedge t^c - r^a{}_i b^i
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msubsup
                    %mi α
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi j
                    %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mi j
                  %mo −
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi c
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{CE(\mathfrak{g})} b^i = -\alpha^i_{a j} t^a \wedge b^j
                  \-
                  r^i{}_{a b c} t^a \wedge t^b \wedge t^c
                  \\,,
          %p
            for collections of structure constants
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{C^a{}_{b c}\}
            (the bracket on
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msubsup
                    %mi r
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{r^i_a\}
            (the differential
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_1 \to \mathfrak{g}_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi α
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\alpha^i{}_{a j}\}
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_0
            on
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{r_{a b c}\}
            (the “Jacobiator” for the bracket on
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_0
          %p
            These constants are subject to constraints (the weak
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+identity"} Jacobi identity
            and its higher
            = succeed "s)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence+law"} coherence law
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (d_{CE(\mathfrak{g})})^2 = 0
                  \\,.
          %p
            Over a test space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            a
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ←
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^\bullet(U) \leftarrow W(\mathfrak{g})
                  \:
                  (A,B)
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{g})
          %p This is given by a 1-form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A \in \Omega^1(U, \mathfrak{g}_0)
          %p and a 2-form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B \in \Omega^2(U, \mathfrak{g}_1)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            of this is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi β
                    %mo ,
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\beta, H)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi β
                    %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi dR
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi c
                  %mo +
                  %msubsup
                    %mi r
                    %mi i
                    %mi a
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\beta^a = d_{dR} A^a + \frac{1}{2}C^a{}_{b c} A^b \wedge A^c
                  + r^{a}_{i} B^i
          %p and whose 3-form component is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi dR
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi i
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi α
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi j
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi j
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi c
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^i
                  \=
                  d_{dR} B^i
                  +
                  \\alpha^i{}_{a j} A^a \wedge B^j
                  +
                  r^i{}_{a b c} A^a \wedge A^b \wedge A^c
                  \\,.
          %h3#differential_ech_cocycle_data Differential Čech cocycle data
          %p
            We spell out the data of a connection on a 2-bundle over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with respect to a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FSS"} FSS
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#SchreiberCohesive"} SchreiberCohesive
          %p (…)
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+string+structure"} differential string structure
                (untwisted) is a 2-connection with coefficients in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+2-group"} string 2-group
                \/
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+Lie+2-algebra"} string Lie 2-algebra
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
                theory of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fivebrane"} fivebrane
                is expected to be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-supersymmetric+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-supersymmetric QFT
                containing a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual higher gauge theory
                whose fields are 2-connections (see
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/NS5-brane#SelfDual2Connections"} Self-dual 2-connections
                there).
            %li
              %p
                A connection on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+vector+bundle"} twisted vector bundle
                is naturally a 2-connection.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection on a bundle
            %li
              %p
                %strong connection on a 2-bundle
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+gerbe"} connection on a gerbe
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle+gerbe"} connection on a bundle gerbe
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid+of+Lie+2-algebra+valued+forms"} 2-groupoid of Lie 2-algebra valued forms
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+3-bundle"} connection on a 3-bundle
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle+2-gerbe"} connection on a bundle 2-gerbe
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} connection on an ∞-bundle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"}> parallel transport
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+parallel+transport"} higher parallel transport
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy"} holonomy
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            Connections on 2-bundles with vanishing 2-form curvature and arbitrary 3-form curvature are defined in terms of their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+parallel+transport"} higher parallel transport
            are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"} Konrad Waldorf
              %p
                %em> Smooth Functors and Differential Forms
                , Homology, Homotopy Appl., 13(1), 143-203 (2011) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0802.0663"}> arXiv:0802.0663
                )
              %p
                %em> Connections on non-abelian gerbes and their holonomy
                , Theory and Applications of Categories, Vol. 28, 2013, No. 17, pp 476-540. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/28/17/28-17abs.html"}> TAC
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0808.1923"} arXiv:0808.1923
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+an+(%E2%88%9E%2C1)-topos+--+references#SchrWalII+III"} web
          %p expanding on
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em Higher gauge theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0511710"}> arXiv:math/0511710
              ) (
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos+--+references/#BaezSchreiber"}> web
              )
          %p
            Much further discussion and illustration and relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+networks"} tensor networks
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Parzygnat18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arthur+Parzygnat"}> Arthur Parzygnat
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Two-dimensional algebra in lattice gauge theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.01139"} arXiv:1802.01139
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1063/1.5078532"} doi:10.1063/1.5078532
          %p
            Examples of 2-connections with vanishing 2-form curvature obtained from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            are discusssed in
          %ul
            %li
              Olivier Brahic,
              %em On the infinitesimal Gauge Symmetries of closed forms
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1010.2189"}> arXiv
              )
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            data for 2-connections with coeffcients in
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+2-group"} automorphism 2-group
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawrence+Breen"}> Lawrence Breen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Messing"} William Messing
                %em Differential Geometry of Gerbes
                Advances in Mathematics, Volume 198, Issue 2, 20 (2005) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0106083"}> arXiv:math/0106083
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawrence+Breen"}> Lawrence Breen
                ,
                %em Differential Geometry of Gerbes and Differential Forms
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0802.1833"}> arXiv:0802.1833
                )
          %p and
          %ul
            %li
              Paolo Aschieri, Luigi Cantini,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Branislav+Jurco"} Branislav Jurco
              %em Nonabelian Bundle Gerbes, their Differential Geometry and Gauge Theory
              , Communications in Mathematical Physics Volume 254, Number 2 (2005) 367-400,(
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0312154"}> arXiv:hep-th/0312154
              ).
          %p A discussion of fully general local 2-connections is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                \-connections
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0801.3480"}> arXiv:0801.3480
              )
          %p and the globalization is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Cech+cocycles+for+differential+characteristic+classes"} Cech cocycles for differential characteristic classes
          %p For a discussion of all this in a more comprehensive context see section xy of
          %ul#SchreiberCohesive
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
          %p
            See also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+infinity-bundle"} connection on an infinity-bundle
            for the general theory.
          %h3#applications_to_physics Applications to physics
          %p
            Nonabelian 2-connections appear for instance as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-fields"} B-fields
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+string+structure"} differential string structure
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} 7-dimensional Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            An appearance in 4-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4d+TQFT"} 4d TQFT
            is reported in
          %ul#GukovKapustin13
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+Gukov"}> Sergei Gukov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Kapustin"} Anton Kapustin
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topological+Quantum+Field+Theory%2C+Nonlocal+Operators%2C+and+Gapped+Phases+of+Gauge+Theories"} Topological Quantum Field Theory, Nonlocal Operators, and Gapped Phases of Gauge Theories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1307.4793"}> arXiv:1307.4793
              )
        .revisedby
          %p
